{
  "_doc": "What the bundled app manifests (manifests/*.json) decide, asserted by packages/client-core/src/fieldPolicy.test.ts and crates/atlas-client (field_policy.rs). `fields`, per real kind and field: the wire kind it travels as since sync protocol 7 (`wire`, null for a kind no manifest names), whether its name goes on the wire instead of an opaque tag (`public`), whether its value is encrypted (`encrypted`), and whether protocol 6 encrypted it (`legacy_encrypted`, which reading rows written before protocol 7 needs). Only a project's deleted_at/archived_at (owner-only, still encrypted) and an attachment's blob_sha/thumb_sha (plaintext blob addresses) are public; journal and vault keep nothing public or plaintext, so the server sees no vault item's type, name, folder, URL, timestamp or secret. `token_policies`: the API token policy of a token for `apps`, the strictest of their manifests' `api_tokens` (`max_lifetime_days` null is no limit; `exclusive`: the server refuses a token naming such an app with any other).",
